Package: bootei
Type: Package
Title: Bootstrap Ensemble Inference for Permutation Tests
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(
        given = "Giovanni",
        family = "Corradini",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        email = "corradini@leibniz-bips.de"
    )
Description: Implements BOOTstrap Ensemble Inference (BOOTEI), a refinement for
    discrete permutation tests in low-resolution regimes such as small samples,
    sparse contingency tables, few outcome levels, and pervasive ties. The method
    preserves the original permutation test statistic and augments it with a
    bootstrap ensemble score used solely for deterministic tie-breaking in the
    permutation reference distribution. By reusing a fixed resampling plan across
    permutations (coupling), BOOTEI retains finite-sample validity under
    exchangeability and yields permutation p-values that are never larger than
    those from the classical permutation test. The package provides permutation
    tests for chi-squared independence, Welch t-test, Spearman correlation, Mann-Whitney, and
    Kruskal-Wallis statistics with optional classical behavior when B <= 1.
